{"family": "tapnext", "task": "tracking", "name": "TAPNext", "plain": "TAPNext (Google DeepMind, 2025): tracks any point through a video, online one frame at a time, as next-token prediction with a ViT + linear-recurrence (RG-LRU) backbone; BootsTAPNext-B and the long-video TAPNext++. Apache-2.0 code and weights.", "summary": "TAPNext (Zholus, Doersch, Yang, Koppula et al., Google DeepMind 2025): tracking any point as next-token prediction. A TRecViT-B (12 blocks, each a gated linear recurrence over time per token and a ViT layer over the tokens of a frame) reads 8 x 8 patches of 256 x 256 frames plus one token per query point and predicts, frame by frame, the point's position (512-bin classification, windowed soft-argmax) and whether it is visible. Online: each frame only sees the past.", "tier": "experimental", "upstream": "https://github.com/google-deepmind/tapnet", "upstream_commit": "ceedd60bb9f6c9f7c74796e4445aff6c6ddf7c9b", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "TAPNext: Tracking Any Point (TAP) as Next Token Prediction", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.05579", "date": "2025-04-08", "venue": "arXiv", "variants": ["tapnext"]}, {"title": "TAPNext++: What's Next for Tracking Any Point (TAP)?", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.10582", "date": "2026-04-12", "venue": "arXiv", "variants": ["tapnext-pp"]}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["fvm_conv"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32", "float16"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "no_original_reason": "", "options": [], "outputs": [{"name": "tracks", "extra": false}, {"name": "visibility", "extra": false}], "output_info": {}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE"], "licence_notes": [], "limitations": ["Online, causal: a point is tracked from its query frame on; in frames before it the model has no information (the tracks there are its guess, with a low visibility). Query on the first frame, or run the reversed video for the backward part.", "Frames are resized to 256 x 256 (the training size), whatever their size and aspect ratio.", "One video per call; all queries of a call share the video."], "task_io": "Input: a video (its frames in order) and query points `(t, x, y)`. Output: the position of every query in every frame and the probability that it is visible there.", "install": {"extras": [], "noncommercial_weights": []}, "variants": [{"id": "tapnext", "released": "0.2.0", "added_in": "0.2.0", "ref": "tapnext@1", "name": "tapnext", "setting": "", "default_tag": false, "params": {}, "licence": {"code": "Apache-2.0", "code_class": "permissive", "weights": "Apache-2.0", "weights_assumed": false, "evidence": "https://github.com/google-deepmind/tapnet/blob/ceedd60bb9f6c9f7c74796e4445aff6c6ddf7c9b/README.md#license-and-disclaimer", "training_data": [{"id": "unstated", "name": "not stated by the authors"}], "training_note": "Upstream: TAPNext is trained on synthetic Kubric MOVi-F sequences and fine-tuned with BootsTAP self-training on unlabelled real videos (not released); TAPNext++ is further fine-tuned on PointOdyssey and Kubric-1024 (1024-frame synthetic sequences). None has a dataset entry here yet.", "commercial": "yes", "reasons": [], "notes": ["data: unstated"]}, "weights": [{"name": "bootstapnext_ckpt.npz", "sha256": "19de6b1495555c2afb4b56e823a3f3c2fd7236eea05c53d98feab3cccd1b4a28", "size": 776980182, "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/dm-tapnet/tapnext/bootstapnext_ckpt.npz", "host": "Google Drive", "member": null, "archive_size": null, "mirror": null}], "input_size": "any H x W >= 32, padded to a multiple of 32", "tested_max": {"size": "3000x4000", "alloc_mib": 4429, "reserved_mib": 4570}, "speed": {"standard": "480x854", "inputs": [{"input": "480x854", "scene": "synthetic", "standard": true, "modes": {"original16": {"ms": 908.79, "ms_min": 669.59, "runs": 5, "peak_alloc_mb": 1721, "peak_reserved_mb": 1902, "load_s": 13.06, "first_call_s": 0.903, "scene": "synthetic (fastfo